# A unified diff represents a blank context line as a single space, which
# `git diff --check` reports as trailing whitespace — so `make check-whitespace`
# fails on any patch containing one. Stripping it would corrupt the patch.
#
# Exempt patch files from whitespace checking. They are machine-generated and
# must be byte-exact for `git apply` to accept them.
*.patch -whitespace
*.diff  -whitespace
